{"title":"2020 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Trigonometry_Identities)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Trigonometry Identities)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Calculus_finish)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Calculus finish)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Calculus_Finish)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Calculus Finish)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_On_The_Spot_STEM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by On The Spot STEM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d3083d1692bad42166a441dc3293eda390788a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq a \\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />, let numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be chosen independently at random from the intervals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7d05d4da0d50abf77ee166ae0c6474bee5a1cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, a]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab178d831a786b92cb4c9ddc2d33578223036f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />, respectively, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac37e8ff9aeea3ac5eaf42779864032eb645c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> be the probability that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dda018877a7b217408e61c488287f3bb9d31582.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^2{(\\pi x)} + \\sin^2{(\\pi y)} &gt; 1\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />\nWhat is the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc203907a2faff74b09a5108a894bd0f6642bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/7229dbda36c22f3c7a4aad5e76338000284c8e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{7}{12} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 - \\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}-1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"512\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's start first by manipulating the given inequality.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/8/cb8efe9949fa008c546e52b562015960b29b76f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^{2}{(\\pi x)}+\\sin^{2}{(\\pi y)}&gt;1\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3e20e036a736e493cf3d41f17f106a79f6ebc86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^{2}{(\\pi x)}&gt;1-\\sin^{2}{(\\pi y)}=\\cos^{2}{(\\pi y)}\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let's consider the boundary cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/17557408fa78ab42e49c5f64481891d3ffac07b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(\\pi x)}=\\pm \\cos{(\\pi y)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93ef44e6b1df372b5c977cd09b9ef7f5d1ae6ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{(\\pi x)}=\\pm \\cos{(\\pi y)}=\\sin{(\\tfrac 12 {\\pi}\\pm \\pi y)}\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Solving the first case gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b25d7cd56a6d0c43ef832495aab8ab53a5f7e05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\tfrac{1}{2}-x \\quad \\textrm{and} \\quad  y=x-\\tfrac{1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"21\" /> Solving the second case gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e2834ef3bae5c13dd5fb8845ce37722f9b42436e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=x+\\tfrac{1}{2}\\quad \\textrm{and} \\quad y=\\tfrac{3}{2}-x.\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"21\" /> If we graph these equations in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6aa56acfcb95ab5be4a1c4210c59219c425167b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,1]\\times[0,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, we get a rhombus shape. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d922c21d526814bbd9d43648760262218cf640.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(9)+0.8); size(200); pen p=fontsize(10); pair A,B,C,D,A1,A2,B1,B2,C1,C2,D1,D2,I,L; A=MP(&quot;(0,0)&quot;,origin,down+left,p); B=MP(&quot;(1,0)&quot;,right,down+right,p); C=MP(&quot;(1,1)&quot;,right+up,up+right,p);  D=MP(&quot;(0,1)&quot;,up,up+left,p); A1=MP(&quot;&quot;,extension(A,B,(0.5,0),(0,0.5)),2*down,p); dot(A1); A2=MP(&quot;&quot;,extension(A,D,(0.5,0),(0,0.5)),2*left,p); dot(A2); B1=MP(&quot;&quot;,extension(B,C,(0.5,0),(0,-0.5)),2*right,p); dot(B1); B2=MP(&quot;&quot;,extension(C,D,(0.5,1),(0,0.5)),2*up,p); dot(B2); real a=0.7; draw(A1--B1--B2--A2--cycle, gray+0.6); draw(a*right--a*right+up, royalblue); draw(A1--B2, royalblue+dashed); draw(A--B--C--D--A, black+1.2); dot(&quot;$(a,0)$&quot;,(a,0),down); dot(&quot;$(a,1)$&quot;,(a,1),up); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"295\" />\nTesting points in each section tells us that the inside of the rhombus satisfies the inequality in the problem statement.\n</p><p>From the region graph, notice that in order to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac37e8ff9aeea3ac5eaf42779864032eb645c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/75629ef9d465220e558e8dc7b8ec12fe3c437fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq\\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"46\" height=\"23\" />. We can solve the rest with geometric probability.\n</p><p>Instead of maximizing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac37e8ff9aeea3ac5eaf42779864032eb645c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, we minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e020ca867d2caec0fe8b51b6d12d0c92642b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(a)=1-P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd06d465665181cb95333f18ab4ca802d5ffb815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> consists of two squares (each broken into two triangles), one of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84a414e9655bf25b41aebc8c9f7bcb651acf2fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> and another of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f47c6533644032aea376b5f4d4d1a2add73eda1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-\\tfrac 12)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"66\" height=\"23\" />. To calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd06d465665181cb95333f18ab4ca802d5ffb815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, we divide this area by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081895533609872b95d9f66fc1fc82b496c8a642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q(a) = \\frac{1}{a}\\left(\\frac{1}{4}+(a-\\tfrac 12)^2\\right) = \\frac{1}{a}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+a^2-a\\right)= a+\\frac 1{2a}-1.\\]\" width=\"468\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>By AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/795338420a95ff516a71c53cddb71aeb247ddab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+\\frac{1}{2a}\\geq 2\\sqrt{\\frac{a}{2a}}=\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"177\" height=\"43\" />, which we can achieve by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/4601a5c2ee9625a8c361176435d3df8737534056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac37e8ff9aeea3ac5eaf42779864032eb645c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7ff90d5dedb7340c9f9f5d3296e56fd4fd373e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\min(Q(a))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec55f508a8cdcfc542892243d97536aa8aca33e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-(\\sqrt{2}-1) =\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 - \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"228\" height=\"35\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Trigonometry_Identities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Trigonometry_Identities)\">Solution 2 (Trigonometry Identities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Trigonometry Identities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d9cf8dcfaddae79ba1760b160e9959d26ba1d86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^2{(\\pi x)} + \\sin^2{(\\pi y)} &gt; 1, \\quad \\sin^2{(\\pi x)} - (1 - \\sin^2{(\\pi y)} ) &gt; 0, \\quad \\sin^2{(\\pi x)} - \\cos^2{(\\pi y)} &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"637\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/7275135d8f7ab2a4c8dedc9f3888d2515e75d9bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[( \\sin{(\\pi x)} + \\cos{(\\pi y)} )(\\sin{(\\pi x)} - \\cos{(\\pi y)})&gt; 0, \\quad \\left( \\sin{(\\pi x)} + \\sin{( \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y)} \\right) \\left( \\sin{(\\pi x)} - \\sin{(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y)} \\right)&gt; 0\\]\" width=\"798\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/3286fae5b4128443231db6fbb5f24930b3ea7a83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sin{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y }{2} \\right)} \\cos{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y }{2} \\right)} 2 \\sin{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y }{2} \\right)} \\cos{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y }{2} \\right)} &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"683\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7345d267acc54c55f633516d9d9a729495af81ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sin{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y }{2} \\right)} \\cos{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y }{2} \\right)} 2 \\sin{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y }{2} \\right)} \\cos{\\left( \\frac{ \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y }{2} \\right)} &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"683\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfba9b81fab4e347abff00699e4024b58b973107.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{\\left(\\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y\\right)} \\sin{\\left( \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y \\right)} &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac9e2cc890d0e92b85dabbdbc1f8f39d3eeda7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\left(\\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y\\right)} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f188c552d1659f078267f30f34657fbdec707b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\left( \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y \\right)} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e8046a5f5ffcfbf1c13345f2cbfb5c2857a4d64a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; \\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y &lt; \\pi \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 0 &lt; \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y &lt; \\pi\\]\" width=\"399\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/832219f3ed06bb4a5dd13b9744d09ff809303faf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; x + \\frac{1}{2} - y &lt; 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 0 &lt; x - \\frac{1}{2} + y &lt; 1\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c5573c94c0d263e397afb95a4ada87844e84ea1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x - \\frac{1}{2} &lt; y &lt; x + \\frac{1}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -x + \\frac{1}{2} &lt; y &lt; -x + \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"393\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6e7a7c13abb060cc0a8c98ee8b56b1fec828f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\left(\\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y\\right)} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbcfeab7d8acc844b300979413e3fbf0c379e4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\left( \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y \\right)} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02a3486edea33802e586e5b0ec74c49acf155542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi &lt; \\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y &lt; 2\\pi \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\pi &lt; \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y &lt; 2\\pi\\]\" width=\"421\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/6069390d10ab9f07821b1a42ab7a545643928a6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 &lt; x + \\frac{1}{2} - y &lt; 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 1 &lt; x - \\frac{1}{2} + y &lt; 2\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1f158598120149d96093309cc83c457a53a7d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x - \\frac{3}{2} &lt; y &lt; x - \\frac{1}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -x + \\frac{3}{2} &lt; y &lt; -x + \\frac{5}{2}\\]\" width=\"393\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6e7a7c13abb060cc0a8c98ee8b56b1fec828f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\left(\\pi x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\pi y\\right)} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbcfeab7d8acc844b300979413e3fbf0c379e4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\left( \\pi x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi y \\right)} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"35\" /> cannot be true, because that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e0fb93486b514b62f25bbf3c4724b4e53b3d36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1, 2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is in the the boundaries <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230d53a7c5d2151169a24a8f893ae06e5d0639cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - \\frac{1}{2} &lt; y &lt; x + \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bbdaef9ce61c79144610d47b9c141a3ab5dac38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x + \\frac{1}{2} &lt; y &lt; -x + \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Finishing like Solution 1, 3, or 4 gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/8959cb3c3badc49fff7652c1aa81db424b50e5a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a) =\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 - \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"165\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Calculus_finish.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Calculus_finish)\">Solution 3 (Calculus finish)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Calculus finish)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We find the same region as in the first solution or the second solution, and again notice we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/3222a9c3bbae567a74a1d0c1a2b8c21bcacfffda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\geq \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>We now express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as a function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563eda72ac38adb42e43397f636f21d9fe04ba56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=(1-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />. The triangle on the right of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741720281e465fc7461c32d504f6d54c5bcaff7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is an isosceles right triangle with altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, so it has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />. The total area of the region to the left of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741720281e465fc7461c32d504f6d54c5bcaff7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b4b97b1c35ed15d859889c4fd2c12d8e985ff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. So \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af3c54128994fb71522cff8f4346148b84c28bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(b) = \\frac{1/2 - b^2}{1-b}\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"39\" />\nDifferentiating using the quotient rule, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has local extrema at\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/addfc1f25ea2531f7e8cf9649bb5339cb9e39045.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P&#39;(b) = \\frac{(1-h)(-2h)-(-1/2 - h^2)(-1)}{(1-h)^2} = 0\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"44\" />\nSetting the numerator equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and solving the quadratic, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has extrema at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55558cbdbc6f9fd2f75f1b1e62efb10c1998421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1 \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" />. Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8d80767380a780290d8170ad74f97c220dc8bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1-\\frac{\\sqrt 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" /> is within the desired region. Plugging in, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/1425e6a00198ad6818ff9a9277cdcff8ca427933.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1-\\frac{\\sqrt 2}{2}) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 - \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"215\" height=\"43\" /> as our solution. We also need to check <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c18188f6b20e100c99830746cf68df0ca5b07ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(b=0) = 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e657777674283a40ce46cba060b6bc760500ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2 &lt; 2 - \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"24\" />, and if this isn't immediately obvious, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> isn't an answer choice anyways. \n</p><p>~jd9 (AMGM scary)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Calculus_Finish.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Calculus_Finish)\">Solution 4 (Calculus Finish)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Calculus Finish)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We find the same region as in the first solution or the second solution, and again notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/3222a9c3bbae567a74a1d0c1a2b8c21bcacfffda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\geq \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The numerator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac37e8ff9aeea3ac5eaf42779864032eb645c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is the area of the triangle with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/3/4334a700c3de1ac55a722636085628034f255284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, \\frac12), (\\frac12, 0), (\\frac12, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" /> plus the area of the rectangle with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fb3a9f03ec610a885661f9d67d4a09a47418a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac12,0), (a,0), (a,1), (\\frac12,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"197\" height=\"38\" /> subtract the area of the isosceles right triangle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da99bbfc0d4ba9c07ad6515f7d16cc63ba1e196d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a, y=0,x - \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" /> and the isosceles right triangle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b875324b82cf23f0d36b3c615181a8ee02bfb161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a, y=1, -x + \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />. The denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac37e8ff9aeea3ac5eaf42779864032eb645c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is the area of rectangle with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cdeeb5a29fc11f6704099a4113aaedb050accd92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0), (a,0), (a,1), (0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f910c982b74cd2e0db8d7ef707e5a0b4aceea1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(a) = \\frac{ \\frac14 + a - \\frac12 -(a - \\frac12)^2 }{a} = \\frac{a - \\frac14 -a^2 + a - \\frac14 }{a} = \\frac{-a^2 + 2a - \\frac12 }{a} = -a + 2 - \\frac{1}{2a}\\]\" width=\"641\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>By the power rule, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6586a61d9f27a5226729d3b1cd0c1e79852ce46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;(a) = -1 - \\frac12(-1)\\frac{1}{a^2} = -1 + \\frac{1}{2a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"285\" height=\"38\" />. Solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3ef5ab92952784f84c423959835ccdc447f0db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;(a) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb6e0562971c09112facea9c18749c117eb8236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{ \\sqrt{2} }{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754f2546b1cf2596d435dcec4ad904924cfa7de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\because P&#39;(a) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb6e0562971c09112facea9c18749c117eb8236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{ \\sqrt{2} }{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f53ca5aaab76b28dc85ce560cb806f9d99756c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> is positive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81bd7fb7c973301eed5d32fc62bd6a2008e556a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac{ \\sqrt{2} }{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f53ca5aaab76b28dc85ce560cb806f9d99756c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> is negative when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55503e95e6f6d7b9c5e5a12bc2de9948d1d4ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; \\frac{ \\sqrt{2} }{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324a4adb15b36a96f1036a42dbaf7395b95c4a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> has a local maximum when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb6e0562971c09112facea9c18749c117eb8236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{ \\sqrt{2} }{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129c6e3d18e6c6dc065e0498bad01093419fbb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(\\frac{ \\sqrt{2} }{2}) = - \\frac{\\sqrt{2} }{2} + 2 - \\frac{1}{2 \\cdot  \\frac{\\sqrt{2} }{2}} =\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 - \\sqrt{2}}\\]\" width=\"349\" height=\"50\" /> \n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Calculus)\">Solution 5 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Comparing the diagram of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b14656625630b5a99e455eb0af5949d0c1f92758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^{2}{(\\pi x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/6576eabc134e4a0e0d9ccf78cb0e867c911feecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^{2}{(\\pi y)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />, we can see if we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/136c94ca22c1842e19e5e081a9828ac954cfdd3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=k$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8c7ce1d1e0b05b531fca69644c2f55b6a1fcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\in (0+\\lvert \\dfrac{1}{2}-k\\rvert,1-\\lvert\\dfrac{1}{2}-k\\rvert)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"229\" height=\"38\" /> will satisfy the above inequality.\n</p><p>Thus, we can write that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed8b583b138058ca2e2e149da92e3ddf6c60ced.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(a) = \\frac{1}{a} (\\int_0^{a}1-2\\lvert\\frac{1}{2}-x\\rvert{\\rm d}x)\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/35080dfa80d5a3123489ed6ca848ad47547759f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(a) = \\frac{1}{a} (\\int_0^{\\frac{1}{2}}2x{\\rm d}x + \\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{a}2-2x{\\rm d}x) = -a+2-\\frac{1}{2a}\\]\" width=\"405\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Then it is easy to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac37e8ff9aeea3ac5eaf42779864032eb645c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3408cdd947b74d7b9d3bca734c07c220ff16c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />, which give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e452a95e93c5c75cf316dad785ecabd0ce62c839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 - \\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~ERiccc\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MOP 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=qcyHncpasls\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=qcyHncpasls</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_On_The_Spot_STEM\">Video Solution by On The Spot STEM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by On The Spot STEM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5goLUdObBrY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5goLUdObBrY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B\">2020 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\"